    <div class="policy-section">
      <h2>How to measure</h2>
      <div>
        <ul style="padding-left:1.25rem;list-style:disc;display:grid;gap:.375rem;">
          <li><strong>Chest:</strong> lay a similar garment flat and measure across, just under the armholes — then double it.</li>
          <li><strong>Length:</strong> from the highest point of the shoulder straight down to the hem.</li>
          <li><strong>Waist:</strong> across the top of the waistband, doubled.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Easiest method: measure a garment you already own and love the fit of, then match it to the chart.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="policy-section">
      <h2>Between two sizes?</h2>
      <div>
        <p>Our tops are cut relaxed/oversized, so go with the smaller size if you want a regular fit, and the larger one for a roomier look. Still unsure? Message us from the <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/contact" style="color:var(--color-volt);text-decoration:underline;">contact page</a> — tell us your usual size and we'll recommend one.</p>
